# Redoubt isolation-media-drain-backport.patch  (Android, android.txt, 158.0-2)
# Owner: LW-M7-50. BACKPORT of upstream bug 1987001, made conditional on the
# Redoubt isolation gate.
#
#   Bug 1987001 - Improve draining in FFmpegVideoDecoder and FFmpegAudioDecoder
#   on Android. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski
#   Author: Andrew Osmond <aosmond@mozilla.com>, 2026-10-05
#   mozilla-firefox commit 5cf346157068a285144cfb2f0409e81a2796ac59 (Firefox 159)
#   Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329595
#   Upstream patch sha256 (github.com/.../commit/<sha>.patch, fetched 2026-10-10):
#   8d7cc715260958f792d83a2aa26b3bfb01aa20fef0d4ee19d86683d7f8faa2ec
#
# Why: with isolated content (Android 12+), H.264/AAC decode through ffvpx's NDK MediaCodec
# wrapper. In 158 that wrapper completes a drain while MediaCodec still holds
# frames (an output format change before the first frame, or no free output
# buffer until the compositor releases one), so the last frames of a stream are
# lost and a SHORT clip may show no frame at all (upstream commit message).
# Upstream's own isolated-process configuration (bug 1988531) runs with this fix
# in 159; a 158 dot release with isolation on must carry it too.
#
# GATED (owner decision 2026-10-11, "158.0-2, Android 12+ only": Android 8-11
# must behave as 158.0-1). Upstream's change is not limited to MediaCodec: on
# every Android build it also changes SOFTWARE ffvpx decoding (the video
# decoder's AVERROR_EOF-on-send mapping, which 158 has inverted: NOT_AVAILABLE
# without MediaCodec becomes END_OF_STREAM; the audio decoder's repeated empty
# drain packet; flush/shutdown rejecting a pending drain promise). So every
# changed path is conditional on FFmpegDataDecoder::mDrainFixEnabled, read once
# per decoder from StaticPrefs::media_redoubt_isolation_media_enabled(), the
# locked gate pref the other isolation patches read (defined in
# isolation-media-codecs-in-content.patch, set by isolation-media-prefs.patch;
# true exactly when content runs isolated, i.e. Android 12+).
#
# Gate FALSE (Android 8-11), path by path, the branch 158.0 takes:
#   FFmpegDataDecoder::ProcessDrain    no CancelDrainTimer() (and no timer is
#                                      ever armed: MaybeDeferDrain() is only
#                                      called on gated paths)
#   FFmpegDataDecoder::ProcessFlush/   no RejectIfExists(), no timer cancel;
#     ProcessShutdown                  the rest is 158.0's body
#   FFmpegAudioDecoder::Init (hw)      mIsMediaCodec stays false
#   FFmpegAudioDecoder::ProcessFlush   = FFmpegDataDecoder::ProcessFlush() (the
#                                      override only forwards)
#   FFmpegAudioDecoder send packet     every packet is sent, the empty drain
#                                      packet each time, same switch as 158.0;
#                                      mHasSentDrainPacket never set
#   FFmpegAudioDecoder EAGAIN          no drain deferral
#   FFmpegVideoDecoder send EOF        158.0's mapping, verbatim
#   FFmpegVideoDecoder receive EAGAIN  return NS_OK at once
#   FFmpegVideoDecoder::ResumeDrain    158.0's body, verbatim (now an override
#                                      of the new virtual; only callers are
#                                      158.0's QueueResumeDrain and the gated
#                                      drain timer)
#   FFmpegVideoDecoder::MaybeQueueDrain 158.0's condition, verbatim
# Gate TRUE (Android 12+): upstream's code, unchanged in effect.
#
# Upstream files touched (all six of the upstream commit)
# -------------------------------------------------------
#   dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegAudioDecoder.cpp, .h
#   dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegDataDecoder.cpp, .h
#   dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp, .h
#
# How the backport differs from upstream: (1) the gate above; (2) upstream adds
# `mHasSentDrainPacket = false;` to an FFmpegAudioDecoder::ProcessFlush()
# override that 158.0 does not have (upstream added it in between, for
# mInputTimes, which 158 also lacks), so the backport adds that override with
# only the drain reset, declared in the .h; it calls
# FFmpegDataDecoder::ProcessFlush() exactly as upstream's does. Inside the
# gate-true branches the code is upstream's, line for line.
#
# Drop this patch at the Firefox 159 rebase (the fix is upstream there), and
# with it the gate: 159 software ffvpx then behaves as upstream.
#
--- a/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegAudioDecoder.cpp
